Subject: [PATCH] Custom shapes: batch instances into one upload per shape

A custom shape can draw up to 1024 instances per frame. Each instance uploaded
its fill and outline separately, rebound programs and vertex arrays and set the
same uniforms again, and the GPU driver revalidated its state at every draw
call: on an NVIDIA SHIELD this per-instance overhead was about half of the
render thread's time with shape-heavy presets.

The instances are now evaluated in the same order and their geometry collected
into batches (outlines as vertices in the border color, in the same buffer as
the fills); each batch is uploaded once (orphaning the buffer) and drawn in
instance order, setting uniforms once per frame and the blend function only
when it changes. The draw order, and therefore the image, is unchanged.

---
